			"Message": "docs(LICENSE): Migrate from CC0 to Land Public License v1.0\n\nReplaced CC0 1.0 Universal public domain dedication with new Land Public License (LPL) v1.0. This establishes copyleft requirements for the Land project while maintaining compatibility with permissively licensed external works.\n\nKey changes include:\n- Introduces strong copyleft for Land-licensed components\n- Requires attribution and source code availability\n- Defines explicit separation between LPL-covered work and external components\n- Adds patent grants with defensive termination\n- Specifies Bulgarian jurisdiction for disputes\n- Includes compatibility provisions for combining with GPLv3+/AGPLv3+/EUPL/MPL-2.0\n\nThis aligns with Land's goals to foster open collaboration while ensuring contributions remain available under reciprocal terms. The LPL provides clearer governance for the Tauri-based code editor's ecosystem compared to public domain dedication.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: License change from public domain (CC0) to copyleft (LPL) fundamentally alters distribution terms. All contributors must now comply with LPL's reciprocity requirements.",
